description:
Implement `useIntersectionPage` for infinite scroll. When a sentinel element (attached via `ref`) enters the viewport, `fetchMore` is called. The hook tracks `loading` state and a `done` flag that prevents further fetches.

**Example:**
```tsx
function Feed() {
  const fetchNextPage = async () => {
    const data = await api.getPage(page + 1);
    if (data.length === 0) markDone();
    else setItems(prev => [...prev, ...data]);
  };

  const { ref, loading, done } = useIntersectionPage(fetchNextPage);

  return (
    <ul>
      {items.map(item => <li key={item.id}>{item.title}</li>)}
      {!done && <li ref={ref}>{loading ? 'Loading...' : 'Scroll for more'}</li>}
    </ul>
  );
}
```

